-- title:
--   The translated corner detects the total displacement
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be the restricted-product measure of the construction, $S$ its distinguished finite corner, and $S_h=\{x:x+h\in S\}$ for an absolutely summable real sequence $h$. Then
--   $$M(S_h)=M(S)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\sum_n h_n=0.$$
--   This converts preservation of corner mass into the zero-sum constraint on the translation parameter.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Comparisons of benchmark equivalence relations, Theorem 1.5 (formerly MeasureEquivalence.tex, Theorem 1.3); supporting declaration MeasureEquivalenceRestrictedPhase.translatedCorner_mass_eq_base_iff in RestrictedTranslatedCorner.lean, lines 48–64; local source SHA-256 ac39d78690d8e55bdc1bc33a4bde0624d5dd1ad42d4243c680a7abfcd827da62. Designated upload repository: https://github.com/RayjunWang/Benchmark (no source commit published yet).

